Immutable canonical memory bundles now lend verified payload bytes to
transient title consumers instead of allocating a second payload buffer.
Native file-backed reads retain bounded owned snapshots; the existing
owned-read API still provides independent storage. Both paths verify
payloads against pinned descriptors on every read. Inline regressions
cover borrowed shared objects, independent owned reads, replacement and
base selection, and corruption rejection without fallback.

