Browser pointer capture can synchronously focus the canvas and dispatch
a nested lifecycle observation. When the DOM queue is already full, the
nested callback must cancel mouse holds without borrowing state that the
outer pointer callback still owns. The shared browser input adapter now
keeps its bounded button bitset in a Cell, allowing cancellation during
capture and clearing a press rejected by the overflowed queue.

